refactor: give the activity feed an explicit page envelope

The feed returned a serialised Spring Page, so the client read data.content
and data.last. Those are PageImpl serialisation details rather than an API
contract: a Spring Data upgrade, a @JsonIgnore on the type, or a move to a
cursor-based repository would silently change the wire shape and break the
"load older" button with no test failure to point at it.

ActivityPageResponse now owns the shape ({items, hasMore, nextPage, total})
and derives hasMore from !isLast(), so a request past the end reports
terminal instead of sending the client one more round trip. total is new and
is what a "1-30 of 44" footer needs.

The controller also duplicated the membership check and the repository query
that ActivityLogService.getActivityFeed already performed, making that method
dead code. The controller now delegates, and the service keeps the check
next to the query it guards, matching how the other services own their
authorization. Verified live: the response carries exactly the four new
fields with no content/last, pages cover 36 rows without overlap, and
non-member and anonymous requests still return 403 and 401.